      "message": "I can see arguments for keeping this new `.gni` file, or removing it.\n\nI see that `skia_encode_rust_png_srcs` in `core.gni` covers the new location of `SpanUtils.h`, so everything works okay today.  And I think it should be okay to do the same thing when depending on `SpanUtils.h` from new, BMP-related code.\n\nI also note that even before this CL `UtilsForFFI.h` would appear on **two** `.gni` lists (`skia_encode_rust_png_srcs` in `core.gni` and `skia_codec_rust_png` in `codec.gni`).  So having a header in two `.gni` lists seems ok (or at least it doesn\u0027t cause any trouble today).\n\nSo, for simplicity, maybe we should avoid adding `gn/rust_shared_cpp_sources.gni` for now?  We can always do it in a separate CL later / when it is actually needed?\n\n-----------------\n\nIf we _do_ want to add `gn/rust_shared_cpp_sources.gni` (which I try to argue against above), then I have a question: How was this file generated?  This file isn\u0027t mentioned in the changes I see in `bazel/exporter_tool/main.go`, so I don\u0027t think that `make -C bazel generate_gni` would have generated the new file.  But maybe I am missing something?",
